From: HAOS Radxa ZERO 3W fork
Subject: [PATCH] bsp: power on the Bluetooth subsystem at init

The AIC8800 Bluetooth core only answers on its UART once the BT firmware
(fw_adid / fw_patch / fw_patch_table) has been pushed to it over SDIO.
That push is what aicbsp_set_subsys(AIC_BLUETOOTH, AIC_PWR_ON) does.

Upstream only performs it when the module is built with
CONFIG_PLATFORM_ROCKCHIP, which also drags in -DANDROID_PLATFORM and a set
of hard-coded toolchain paths from the upstream author workstation.  We
build with the portable CONFIG_PLATFORM_UBUNTU profile instead, so the
call is compiled out and Bluetooth stays dark even though the hardware and
the device tree are both fine.

Drop the guard.  On a board without a BT core the subsystem power request
simply fails and WiFi is unaffected.

--- a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c
+++ b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c
@@ -440,9 +440,7 @@
 	}
 
 	mutex_init(&aicbsp_power_lock);
-#if defined CONFIG_PLATFORM_ROCKCHIP || defined CONFIG_PLATFORM_ROCKCHIP2
 	aicbsp_set_subsys(AIC_BLUETOOTH, AIC_PWR_ON);
-#endif
 	return 0;
 }
 
